Modifications: the files were modified. The upstream godot-shaders skill was
rewritten in the house style as SKILL.md; its shading-language reference and
the engine-neutral shader-programming skill were merged into
references/fundamentals.md, with the HLSL material cut to a porting table;
GodotPrompter's shader recipes, post-processing, stencil, compositor and
Shader Baker notes became references/recipes.md and references/advanced.md;
its particles-vfx skill became references/particles.md. Only GDScript and
shader examples were kept (C# dropped). Facts were rechecked against the Godot
4.7 docs, the 4.7 migration guide, PRs and the 4.7-stable engine source.
Fixed on port: TIME described as ever-growing (it wraps every 3600 s by
default), the particle "color overrides color_ramp" row (they multiply; the
real trap is a 3D draw material without vertex_color_use_as_albedo), the
"attractor interaction is off" row (it defaults on), fixed_fps defaulting to
30 rather than 0, amount_ratio as a performance lever (it saves nothing),
freeing one-shot particles on a timer (use the finished signal), the claim
that the Shader Baker runs under --headless (it doesn't), and a CompositorEffect
note crediting SDFGI and VoxelGI to the compositor (dropped). Cross-references
were renamed to adminhead plugins (godot, godot-physics, godot-export,
game-performance).
